# ── §FIX-LINE-ENDING-DRIFT (L-802g, 2026-08-09) ──────────────────────────────
#
# THE DEFECT: with no line-ending policy and core.autocrlf=false, an editor that
# writes CRLF into an LF-committed file produces a WHOLE-FILE diff. During the
# 2026-08-09 audit session this happened twice and had to be hand-corrected
# before committing — one raked-wall change showed as 830 changed lines instead
# of 85. A diff nobody can read is a diff nobody reviews, which is a quiet way to
# ship an unreviewed change.
#
# WHY THIS IS SCOPED, AND NOT `* text=auto`
# -----------------------------------------
# The obvious fix is one line, `* text=auto`, and it is wrong here. Measured on
# this repo it renormalises **8,890 files** — overwhelmingly `.agents/`
# transcripts and `attached_assets/` pastes, none of which anyone diffs — in a
# single commit that would blow away `git blame` across the whole tree. That is a
# repo-wide reformatting decision; it is not a line-ending fix, and folding it
# into an unrelated change is exactly the sort of unreviewable edit this program
# exists to stop.
#
# Scoped to the extensions people actually read diffs of, the same fix touches
# **20 files** (renormalised in the commit that introduced this block, so no
# future author is ambushed by it mid-feature).
#
# Explicit `text eol=lf` per extension rather than `text=auto`: no content
# sniffing, so no chance of a binary being mangled by a heuristic. Anything not
# listed here keeps today's behaviour exactly.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
